    },
    {
      "id": "el-1072",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#332a66",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 8497087,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 112374217,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "text",
      "x": 132,
      "y": 12538,
      "width": 805.2,
      "height": 105,
      "text": "WHY THIS IS THE RIGHT ANSWER RATHER THAN A COP-OUT\nPopulating every future day with specific ayat would look more satisfying and be a lie — the scheduler picks reviews from\nmeasured decay, and a review 3 weeks out depends on how the next 20 sessions actually go. Showing invented precision would\nbreak the same honesty contract as §10's retention numbers and §14's 'never shorten the date to motivate'.\n\nThe learner still gets what they asked for — PREDICTABILITY — because the COMMITMENT is stable ('~8 min/day, 1 new ayah')\neven when the item list is not. Predictable EFFORT, honest DETAIL.",
      "originalText": "WHY THIS IS THE RIGHT ANSWER RATHER THAN A COP-OUT\nPopulating every future day with specific ayat would look more satisfying and be a lie — the scheduler picks reviews from\nmeasured decay, and a review 3 weeks out depends on how the next 20 sessions actually go. Showing invented precision would\nbreak the same honesty contract as §10's retention numbers and §14's 'never shorten the date to motivate'.\n\nThe learner still gets what they asked for — PREDICTABILITY — because the COMMITMENT is stable ('~8 min/day, 1 new ayah')\neven when the item list is not. Predictable EFFORT, honest DETAIL.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "el-1073",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1d9e75",
      "backgroundColor": "#e1f5ee",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      },
      "seed": 8505006,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 112478946,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 880,
      "y": 11560,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 204
    },
    {
      "id": "el-1074",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#085041",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 8512925,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 112583675,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "text",
      "x": 892,
      "y": 11572,
      "width": 316.8,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "THE FORECAST IS ALREADY HALF-BUILT\nplanFor() in engine/src/capacity.ts returns\n{ ayahPerDay, etaDays, remaining } from\nremainingAyat + avgWordsPerAyah + minutesPerDay,\nusing Appendix A's cost model\n(T ≈ 0.33·W_new + 0.4·R_due + 1.25·chains\n+ 0.17·junctions).\n\nv3 needs to (a) fix E-06 — divide the budget\nacross ACTIVE SURAHS, not give each the whole\nday — and (b) project etaDays onto a real\ncalendar.",
      "originalText": "THE FORECAST IS ALREADY HALF-BUILT\nplanFor() in engine/src/capacity.ts returns\n{ ayahPerDay, etaDays, remaining } from\nremainingAyat + avgWordsPerAyah + minutesPerDay,\nusing Appendix A's cost model\n(T ≈ 0.33·W_new + 0.4·R_due + 1.25·chains\n+ 0.17·junctions).\n\nv3 needs to (a) fix E-06 — divide the budget\nacross ACTIVE SURAHS, not give each the whole\nday — and (b) project etaDays onto a real\ncalendar.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "el-1075",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#d85a30",
      "backgroundColor": "#faece7",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      },
      "seed": 8520844,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 112688404,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 460,
      "y": 11810,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 249
    },
    {
      "id": "el-1076",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#712b13",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 8528763,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 112793133,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "text",
      "x": 472,
      "y": 11822,
      "width": 316.8,
      "height": 225,
      "text": "HONESTY RULES FOR A FORECAST\n  · Use the learner's MEASURED pace, never the\n    nominal one. planFor() already takes\n    minutesPerDay — feed it observed minutes.\n  · Count ACTIVE days, not calendar days. A\n    learner who drills 4×/week finishes later,\n    and the date must say so.\n  · Re-forecast after every session. A date\n    that never moves is a promise, not a\n    prediction.\n  · Show the assumption INLINE ('1/day, ~6 min')\n    so a slipping date is explainable.\n  · NEVER shorten the date to motivate. That is\n    the one lie that destroys the whole\n    retention-honesty stance in §10.",
      "originalText": "HONESTY RULES FOR A FORECAST\n  · Use the learner's MEASURED pace, never the\n    nominal one. planFor() already takes\n    minutesPerDay — feed it observed minutes.\n  · Count ACTIVE days, not calendar days. A\n    learner who drills 4×/week finishes later,\n    and the date must say so.\n  · Re-forecast after every session. A date\n    that never moves is a promise, not a\n    prediction.\n  · Show the assumption INLINE ('1/day, ~6 min')\n    so a slipping date is explainable.\n  · NEVER shorten the date to motivate. That is\n    the one lie that destroys the whole\n    retention-honesty stance in §10.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "el-1077",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#ba7517",
      "backgroundColor": "#faeeda",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
