    {
      "id": "el-1884",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#712b13",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 14927315,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 197414165,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1272,
      "y": 21272,
      "width": 303.6,
      "height": 225,
      "text": "★ THE FRIEND-STREAK PROBLEM, SOLVED AT THE\nDATA LAYER — not with polite copy.\n\nA shared streak normally makes ANOTHER\nPERSON'S LAPSE YOUR LOSS. That is the exact\nmechanic that manufactures guilt, and guilt is\nwhat sabr jameel exists to prevent.\n\nThe fix: when either person lapses the state\nis simply \"Paused — it resumes when you both\nreturn.\" The UI never says who missed, and the\nother person is NEVER NOTIFIED.\n\nStructurally invisible beats politely worded.\nThere is no copy to get wrong later.",
      "originalText": "★ THE FRIEND-STREAK PROBLEM, SOLVED AT THE\nDATA LAYER — not with polite copy.\n\nA shared streak normally makes ANOTHER\nPERSON'S LAPSE YOUR LOSS. That is the exact\nmechanic that manufactures guilt, and guilt is\nwhat sabr jameel exists to prevent.\n\nThe fix: when either person lapses the state\nis simply \"Paused — it resumes when you both\nreturn.\" The UI never says who missed, and the\nother person is NEVER NOTIFIED.\n\nStructurally invisible beats politely worded.\nThere is no copy to get wrong later.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "el-1885",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#6c5bb8",
      "backgroundColor": "#ece7f8",
