    },
    {
      "id": "el-2425",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#5f5d55",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 19211494,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 254072554,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "text",
      "x": 790,
      "y": 27334,
      "width": 302.5,
      "height": 82.5,
      "text": "· the SEQUENCING state machines (ladder's S1 pass,\n  reconstruct's blankIndex cursor)\n· GRADING — a spec declares no rung, no pretest,\n  no atom, no structured flag\n· the fold (rebuild.ts needs ZERO changes)\n· the 4 render shapes themselves",
      "originalText": "· the SEQUENCING state machines (ladder's S1 pass,\n  reconstruct's blankIndex cursor)\n· GRADING — a spec declares no rung, no pretest,\n  no atom, no structured flag\n· the fold (rebuild.ts needs ZERO changes)\n· the 4 render shapes themselves",
      "fontSize": 11,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "el-2426",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#d85a30",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 19219413,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 254177283,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "text",
      "x": 790,
      "y": 27454,
      "width": 330,
      "height": 25,
      "text": "\"A template that can author a state machine is an\ninterpreter — and an interpreter is where determinism dies.\"",
      "originalText": "\"A template that can author a state machine is an\ninterpreter — and an interpreter is where determinism dies.\"",
      "fontSize": 10,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
