    {
      "id": "el-2730",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#332a66",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 21626789,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 286014899,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1272,
      "y": 32872,
      "width": 310.20000000000005,
      "height": 165,
      "text": "LIFETIME MATH — price it deliberately\n  RM500 ÷ RM20  = 25 months\n  USD200 ÷ USD10 = 20 months\n\nLifetime only pays if learners stay past ~2\nyears — which IS the product thesis (P(recall @\n10y)). It is a coherent bet, not an accident.\n\nBut note the asymmetry: international lifetime\nbreaks even 5 months sooner. If that's not\nintended, RM500/USD250 would align them.",
      "originalText": "LIFETIME MATH — price it deliberately\n  RM500 ÷ RM20  = 25 months\n  USD200 ÷ USD10 = 20 months\n\nLifetime only pays if learners stay past ~2\nyears — which IS the product thesis (P(recall @\n10y)). It is a coherent bet, not an accident.\n\nBut note the asymmetry: international lifetime\nbreaks even 5 months sooner. If that's not\nintended, RM500/USD250 would align them.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
